 "description": "PAID ($0.0045 USDC via x402, paid automatically). Everything about a domain in one call: the registrar, creation and expiry dates, age, status and nameservers from the registry's own RDAP service; live DNS (A, AAAA, MX, NS); email authentication (the SPF record and the DMARC policy); and the TLS certificate port 443 serves \u2014 issuer, validity window, days remaining, whether it covers the name and whether a browser would trust it. Accepts a bare domain or a URL. A TLD whose registry runs no RDAP returns registration null with the reason. A non-existent domain is a paid answer (exists:false); a resolver and registry outage is 502, not charged. Any answer the tool cannot produce is >= 400 and is NOT charged.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "domain": {
    "description": "A domain or a URL (example.com, https://www.example.com/page). Omit the whole body to get the published example (example.com)",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "payment": {
    "description": "Base64 of a single x402 v2 PaymentPayload you signed yourself. OPTIONAL: with AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY set, this tool pays automatically and you never need it. Use it to pay from a DIFFERENT wallet, or when no key is configured \u2014 call once without it to get the 402 (its body carries `howToPay.payloadTemplate`, the exact envelope to sign), then call again with it. When set it is sent as-is as the PAYMENT-SIGNATURE header; no local signing and no price ceiling are applied.",
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "type": "object"
 },
